# DTF tier manifest: upgrade-v156-origin (#2688 — the no-divergence no-op case)
# Profile-set: filesystem / single. Migration-ledger tier; the storage-shape
# upgrade class lives in the `upgrade` tier.
#
# Origin: the published v1.5.6 image. v1.5.6 predates the release/1.5.x
# renumbered slots (v1.5.7 shipped storage_key_index at 154; v1.5.8 shipped
# maven_flat_object_attribution at 155), so its applied ledger — max version
# 153 — is an exact checksum PREFIX of main's chain. Upgrading from it must be
# a pure no-op for the #2686 startup repair (repair_release_1_5_x_divergence
# must NOT fire): the migrator simply applies main's 154+ fresh, the applied
# prefix keeps its original installed_on timestamps, and seeded data survives.
#
# This is the control case for upgrade-v158-origin: it catches BOTH a repair
# that spuriously fires on a clean ancestor ledger AND any future edit to a
# shipped <=153 migration file (which would break every 1.5.x upgrade with a
# VersionMismatch at that slot — the candidate would never reach healthy).
#
# Same two-phase oracle-driven compose pattern as tiers/upgrade.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: several back-to-back logins in seed + oracle.
#
# UPGRADE_OLD_IMAGE: the published, immutable v1.5.6 tag. The oracle asserts
# the origin-ledger signature (max version 153, slot 154 absent) before
# phase 2, so any other image fails loudly.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
UPGRADE_OLD_IMAGE="${UPGRADE_OLD_IMAGE:-ghcr.io/artifact-keeper/artifact-keeper-backend:1.5.6}"
